    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n4 Bed Detached house of c. 172 m² on a corner site with beautiful gardens at the end of a cul-de-sac looking out onto a park green in the village of Keenagh.\n\nOriginally built in 2006 the Cluain Caonach houses were built with a modern architectural style allowing for large rooms and substantial glazing creating bright airy spaces.\n\nThere is large front to rear sitting room with dual aspects ensuring brightness throughout the day. There is a pellet stove that heats this room and some of the adjoining areas. The kitchen dining area has polished porcelain tiled floors and modern kitchen units with breakfast bar and appliances. There are sliding glass doors out to the rear patio area. The tiled floors of the dining area flow into the inner hallway which with the double doors open creates a more open plan feel. There is also a ground floor toilet.\n\nUpstairs the main bedroom is spacious with an ensuite semi tiled shower room. The other 3 bedroom are all double sized and are served by a fully tiled family bathroom that has a very large round Jacussi bath.\n\n\nServices:\n• Mains Water and Sewerage, \n• Oli Fired Central Heating\n• Fibre to the home broadband available\n• Zappi Electric car charger\n\n\nOutside:\nThe house is on a corner site at the end of the cul-de-sac, allowing for a larger garden area that has been lovingly developed by the owner. To the front of the house there is a tarmac drive with parking for at least two cars. There is substantial mature planting to the front and side of the house, creating great privacy.\n\nTo the rear there is a large metal studio shed with power connected, this is situated beside a pond with planted borders. There area a number of other areas in the garden including the rear patio area, vegetable patch growing area and a seated area in the corner of the garden.\n\n\nLocation:\nCluain Caonach is a development of all detached houses, located on the edge of Keenagh, a picturesque village, steeped in history along the Longford / Athlone Road R397.\n\nThe village is convenient to Longford town c. 13 km away and Ballymahon town c. 8 km to the south and Centre Parcs holiday development is just 10 km away.\n\n\nEircode: N39 TX32 \nGPS: 53.6275, -7.8184"
      },
